      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s original site vanished when the railroad bypassed it, prompting a move to a new location two miles east.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chapin%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1872, George Beed and surveyor Ohadiah Smith platted what became known as New Chapin, later dropping the “New.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        5,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
